hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22866","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Uthman, from Khalid ibn Urfutah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O Khalid, indeed there will be after me events and trials and dissension, so if you can be the servant of Allah who is killed, not the killer, then do."
"22867","Hajjaj narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Jami ibn Shaddad, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Yasar, who said: I was sitting with Sulayman ibn Surad and Khalid ibn Urfutah. He said: So they mentioned a man who died of his belly. He said: So it was as though they wished to pray over him. He said: So one of them said to the other: Did not the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever is killed by his belly, he will not be punished in his grave. The other said: Yes."
"22868","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us: Khalid ibn Salamah narrated to us: Muslim, the freedman of Khalid ibn Urfutah, narrated to us that Khalid ibn Urfutah said, and I heard myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah, meaning Muslim, the freedman of Khalid ibn Urfutah, narrated to us that Khalid ibn Urfutah said to al-Mukhtar: This is a liar man, and I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in Hell."
